  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The suggestion that a nation was originally conceived as a body is uncertain. The pride noun may belong with elevation. The key c.bb.af refers to the Goyim ruled by Tidal and is not assigned to the common noun. In 1 Samuel 31 the difference between the living body and a corpse is supplied by the narrative. גֵּו back and midst overlap in surface counts but have distinct senses. SEDRA lexemes 526–529 account for the Syriac forms under גו."
